FAQ = [
 ("What is the best bed rack for a 2016–2023 Tacoma?",
  "For most owners who want a rooftop tent, the RealTruck GoRack. It is a mid-height aluminum and steel rack rated for 1,000 lb static and 600 lb dynamic, with T-slots on all four sides of the side rails, MOLLE side panels and a limited lifetime warranty, and RealTruck lists it from $1,089.99. If you want a brand-name aluminum rack for about half that, the Rough Country 73109 (750 lb static, 400 lb dynamic) is the value pick, but it only fits the 5 ft bed."),
 ("What is the difference between static and dynamic load ratings?",
  "Dynamic is what the rack can carry while the truck is moving, including bumps, braking and body roll. Static is what it can hold while parked, which is the number that matters when people are sleeping in a rooftop tent. The GoRack is rated 1,000 lb static and 600 lb dynamic; the Rough Country 73109 750 lb static and 400 lb dynamic. Your tent plus anything strapped to the rack has to stay under the dynamic figure on the road."),
 ("Does a bed rack need drilling on a 3rd-gen Tacoma?",
  "Often not. The 2016–2023 Tacoma has factory deck rails along the bed sides, and racks like the Thule Xsporter Pro use Tacoma-specific clamps (the XK4 kit) that slide into those tracks. The Rough Country 73109 is different: Rough Country recommends a nutsert tool for the install, and nutserts sit in holes. Read the install sheet for any rack before you buy if you don't want new holes in the composite bed."),
 ("Which rack height is best for a rooftop tent?",
  "Mid-height racks that sit at or just below the cab roof are the usual choice. The tent stays mostly out of the wind behind the cab and the truck is easier to fit in a garage or parking structure. Full-height racks such as the Hooke Road 18.8 in model put the tent level with or above the cab, which gives more room under it for gear. Low racks near 11–13 in suit bikes, boards and a basket more than a tent."),
 ("Will a bed rack fit my 6 ft Tacoma bed?",
  "Only if the listing names the 6 ft bed. The 3rd-gen Tacoma comes with a 5 ft bed (60.5 in) on the Double Cab and a 6 ft bed (73.7 in) on the Access Cab and some Double Cabs. The Rough Country 73109 fits the 5 ft bed only. The Hooke Road 18.8 in rack is listed for the Tacoma 6 ft bed. Measure inside the bed at the rail from the front wall to the closed tailgate before you order."),
 ("Can I run a tonneau cover and a bed rack together?",
  "Only with the right combination. Rough Country says its 73109 does not fit trucks with tri-fold or retractable covers. RealTruck says the GoRack can mount to any bed cover with a T-slot style rail system, such as the RetraxPRO XR, whose T-80851 part adds T-slot rails on the 5 ft Tacoma bed. Yakima sells a Tonneau Kit 1 adapter for its OverHaul HD that names the Retrax XR. Pick the rack and cover as a pair."),
 ("Do 3rd-gen Tacoma bed racks fit the 2024 Tacoma?",
  "Don't assume so. The 2024–2026 Tacoma is an all-new truck, and makers sell separate racks for it: Rough Country lists different part numbers (73141 and 73119) for the 2024–2026 truck than the 73109 for 2005–2023. Some universal clamp racks cover both generations, but buy by the listing that names your model year."),
 ("Do these racks work with Trail Edition bed storage boxes?",
  "The makers we checked don't say. Trail Special Edition and Trail Edition trucks have factory storage boxes in the bed sides, and racks that clamp near the rails can interfere with the box lids. None of the product pages we read address the boxes directly, so ask the seller in writing before you buy a rack for a Trail Edition truck."),
 ("Is a Leitner or Yakima rack worth the extra money?",
  "They cost more for real differences. Leitner lists its ACS Forged for the Tacoma at $2,099 with an 85 lb weight and ratings of 1,400 lb parked static, 800 lb on-road and 400 lb off-road, and it is sold direct rather than on Amazon. Yakima's OverHaul HD towers adjust from 19 to 30 in and are rated 500 lb on-road and 300 lb off-road. Pay for them if you need adjustable height or the highest static rating."),
 ("How much does a bed rack add to a Tacoma's bed weight?",
  "Check the rack's own weight against your payload. Yakima lists the OverHaul HD towers at 59.52 lb before crossbars; Leitner lists the ACS Forged at 85 lb. Add a tent, recovery gear and water, and the total climbs fast on a midsize truck. Look up the payload figure on your door-jamb sticker and subtract passengers before loading the rack."),
]

